# LaTeX build artifacts. main.pdf is regenerable from main.tex plus refs.bib
# with `make`, so it is not committed: a stale PDF in git is worse than none.
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.synctex.gz
*.tmp
*.toc
main.pdf
# The double-blind variant, produced by `make anon`. Derived from the same
# main.tex behind the \anon flag, so committing it would be committing a
# second copy of the manuscript that nothing keeps in step.
anon.pdf

# Figure PNGs are for eyeballing during development only. The PDFs are the
# inputs LaTeX actually uses and they ARE committed, because a figure that
# cannot be rebuilt from a committed source and a committed output is not
# reproducible. make_figures.py regenerates both.
figures/*.png

# Derived arXiv submission package. `make arxiv` rebuilds it from main.tex and
# main.bbl; committing a second copy of the manuscript invites drift.
p2-arxiv-submission.tar.gz
arxiv/
